  // three-by-three block, every row and column that is not an edge, every diagonal of four squares or more. A shape
  // with its discs on it is one of 3^n arrangements (each square empty, Dark or Light), and every arrangement has a
  // number worked out beforehand: how many discs better or worse than level it leaves the side to move at the end
  // of the game, as far as that shape can tell. The numbers were learnt from games (see the head of the file); a
